# Record it in the file (HARD)

Chat is not the record. If a result belongs in a checklist, scorecard, decision log, extraction note, SOP, or launch-status doc, write it there before the turn ends.

## Checklist steps

When a step in [nypllc-90-day-execution-checklist.md](../../nypllc-90-day-execution-checklist.md), or another execution checklist, is fully done:

- Mark that bullet `- [x]` in the same turn.
- Link the evidence file on the same line.
- Leave a partial step `- [ ]`. Do not check a parent package because one bullet inside it is done.

```markdown
- [x] Export advertising cost by date and campaign. Evidence: [weekly SOP](ads-pull-2026-10-18-weekly-sop/WEEKLY-SOP.md).
```

## Numbers and status

When a pull, export, or review changes a figure the business is using, update the file that owns that figure. Do not stop after saying it in the reply.

| Result | Write it in |
|---|---|
| Weekly orders, cash, contribution, ads | `scorecards/` for that week |
| Baseline export totals | the extraction note next to the CSVs |
| A decision that replaces an older plan date or target | `decision-log.md` |
| Ads SOP result | that week's `WEEKLY-SOP.md` and `google_ads_changes.md` |
| A billing or launch fact | the matching CRM status doc |

The Oct 18 miss: $519 per order and $468 after ads were reported in chat only. They belonged in the extraction note and the weekly scorecard in that same turn.
